course: dictionary
lesson: 14378
title: Words for big life events
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a special event, and the words around them tell you what is happening. Look at this: «The ordination service was held in the old church on a sunny Saturday.» Service and church tell you this is a special ceremony in a church.
explain: «After his ordination, Tom became a priest.» The word after shows that the ordination came first, and something new happened to Tom afterwards. So ordination is the ceremony where a person is made a priest. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Words like "ceremony" or "making a priest" would fit.
explain: Ordination can also mean the state of being given a role. «Her ordination meant she was now a minister who could lead the services.» Check it by swapping in your meaning: "her being given the role of a minister" still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: Ordination means the ceremony in which a person is made a priest, minister, deacon or rabbi.
fact: The ceremony is usually led by a bishop or another leader.
fact: Christians believe the person is called by God to serve, so an ordination service is a big, joyful event.
fact: In the news, people sometimes discuss who may be ordained in different churches.
exercise: «The ordination service was held in the old church on a sunny Saturday.» What is an ordination service? | A school sports day | *A ceremony where someone is made a priest or minister | A picnic in the churchyard
exercise: «After his ordination, Tom became a priest.» What does ordination mean here? | A kind of church bell | *The ceremony of making someone a priest | A long walk to church
exercise: In an ordination, who usually leads the ceremony? | A shopkeeper selling candles | The children in the choir | *A bishop or another leader
test: Which phrase names a church ceremony where someone is made a minister? | *ordination service | School bus route | Birthday party
test: «Her ordination meant she was now a minister.» Here ordination means | *being given the role of a minister | The name of a river | A kind of musical instrument
exam: Jayden reads about "the ordination of women" in the news. What does this phrase mean? | A women's football team | *who may be made priests or ministers in that church | A shop that sells hats | Their family birthday party
